#  PlantAI - copy to .env and fill in.
#
#  Organised by WHO READS WHAT:
#    §1  the app  - inlined into the JS bundle at build time, assume public
#    §2  server   - never reaches the phone; in production these are Render secrets
#    §3  tuning   - server only, all optional, sane defaults in code
#
#  Only §1 is read by the app. Since TODOS A3 every provider key lives on the
#  server and the app talks to nothing but the server.


# ══ §1  READ BY THE APP ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time wherever the name appears in source,
#  so everything here ends up inside the bundle. Changing either value requires
#  `expo start --clear` - a plain reload keeps the old value baked in.

#  Where the app sends photos and nursery searches.
#    local   → your Mac's LAN IP, so simulator and device both reach it.
#              Re-check with `ipconfig getifaddr en0`; it moves with DHCP.
#    hosted  → the Render URL, e.g. https://plantai-api.onrender.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:4000

#  Supabase project (issue #1, User Accounts + Settings/Profile). Publishable
#  key only - safe to embed, RLS enforces per-user access at the DB level.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_publishable_key_here

#  SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Service-role key, used by the API server to read and write
#  the shared nursery-scrape cache (public.nursery_searches). It bypasses RLS -
#  never put it in an EXPO_PUBLIC_* name and never ship it to a phone. Leave it
#  unset locally: the cache then does nothing and every search is a live scrape.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_here

#  Sent as the `x-plantai-key` header. Must equal API_SHARED_SECRET in §2 - two
#  halves of one value, split so the server half can be a Render secret while
#  this half is a build constant.
#
#  ⚠️ NOT AUTHENTICATION. It ships inside the bundle by necessity and anyone
#  holding a build can extract it in about a minute. It raises the cost of
#  casual abuse; DAILY_REQUEST_CAP is what actually bounds the bill. Read
#  server/gate.ts before building anything that assumes this endpoint is secure.
#
#  Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_SECRET=generate_one_and_use_the_same_value_below


# ══ §2  READ BY THE SERVER ONLY ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
#  The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix here is vestigial - no app code has read these since
#  A3. It survives because dashboard/server.ts and scripts/scrape-nurseries.ts
#  still read these exact names (TODOS H1). server/index.ts prefers the PLAIN
#  name and falls back to the prefixed one:
#      const env = (k) => process.env[k] || process.env[`EXPO_PUBLIC_${k}`]
#  In production only the plain names exist, set as Render secrets from
#  render.yaml's `sync: false` entries.

#  Server half of the gate secret. Identical to EXPO_PUBLIC_API_SECRET above.
API_SHARED_SECRET=generate_one_and_use_the_same_value_above

#  PlantNet - species identification.  https://my.plantnet.org
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLANTNET_API_KEY=your_plantnet_api_key_here

#  OpenAI - vision health assessment + scraper extraction/verification.
#  https://platform.openai.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

#  Firecrawl - primary nursery page scraper.  https://firecrawl.dev
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=your_firecrawl_api_key_here

#  Tavily Extract - fallback when Firecrawl fails or returns empty. Optional;
#  omit to disable the fallback and the scraper still works.  https://tavily.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_TAVILY_API_KEY=your_tavily_api_key_here

#  Google Places (New) - nursery discovery + the in-app map. Requesting
#  websiteUri bills the Enterprise SKU.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here


# ══ §3  GATE TUNING - server only, all optional ═══════════════════════════════

#  log     = allow everything, record what enforcing would have blocked (default)
#  enforce = actually block
#  Start on `log` only if you have installed builds that predate the secret.
#  This project has no EAS and no installed builds, so `enforce` is correct from
#  the first request - a public billable endpoint in log mode is a stranger's
#  daily cap.
GATE_MODE=enforce

#  Hard ceiling on billable requests per UTC day - the real spend guard. One
#  nursery search = 1 Places call + N Firecrawl scrapes + N OpenAI passes; one
#  diagnosis = 1 PlantNet + 1 OpenAI vision call.
DAILY_REQUEST_CAP=200

#  Per-IP burst limit. Job polling is exempt, or a long scrape polled every few
#  seconds would rate-limit the client out of its own result.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=6

#  Emit CORS headers for this origin only. Unset = no CORS header, which is
#  correct for a native app. Set it only if a browser needs to call the API.
# CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
